The program then prompts the user to input the original file name and the signature file name for verification. It reads the original file content and the digital signature file content, and verifies the digital signature using the public key. The program outputs whether the signature is valid or not.

Note that this is a very basic implementation that doesn't include proper error handling or input validation. A real-world implementation should include these features to ensure the security and reliability of the digital signature.

